# VVNB — 2 real Aireon/ASTERIX-derived arrivals, RWY 11L, both landing & taxiing to Gate 24 area.
# Source: HVN7560 CR-NB.csv (Cam Ranh->Noi Bai, 2025-07-28) and VAG628 DN-NB.csv (Da Nang->Noi Bai, 2025-08-28).
# These are two DIFFERENT real days/flights (no real-world simultaneity claim).
#
# TIMING NOTE / KNOWN CONFLICT RISK: VAG628 CRE is 3:00 after HVN7560's, at the user's explicit request
# (originally 11:00 to fully respect the "never share a taxiway" rule; user asked for 2:30, was warned
# this overlaps, then asked for 3:00 anyway). HVN7560 doesn't reach its gate until ~00:08:30 (est.), so
# with VAG628 touching down ~00:06:30 and taxiing the same route to the same gate area, the two WILL
# likely be on the shared taxiway at the same time around 00:06:30-00:08:30. This is a deliberate,
# accepted risk for this run, not an oversight -- revert to a 9-11 min gap if that's not wanted anymore.
# Ground speeds are read directly in kt (RESGVGroundSpeed once on ground); airborne AGV speed field is
# in NM/s and converted x3600 to kt. The 10NM-1NM final leg for each is NOT in the source data (both
# recordings start well after the real base/turn-in, so a straight-in synthetic leg is used instead,
# same method as the VVDN scenario) -- built along the real RWY11L extended centerline
# (thr 21.2252536,105.7925694, landing hdg 107) on a standard 3 deg glideslope (~318ft/NM).
#
# ROLLOUT FIX: the raw ADS-B fix just before each aircraft's right turn off the runway (VAG628's
# 26kt point, HVN7560's 31kt point) sat close enough off the RWY11L centerline that the straight
# segment leading into it cut across at a visible angle instead of continuing straight down the
# runway. Both are now pinned to 21.2200,105.8110 (on-centerline) so the rollout stays straight
# right up to the real turn point before turning right onto the taxiway.
#
# SPEED UNIT SAGA (final answer, see VVDN scenario header for the full story): values below are plain
# physical knots, NOT divided. A prior edit divided by 1.94384 to fix the waypoint-label display, but
# that made the AIRCRAFT ITSELF fly at real half-speed (confirmed unrealistic, ~90kt at 1600ft on a
# VVDN approach) -- BlueSky's live flight dynamics track this file's SPD directly and correctly as
# knots, so correct physics wins over a cosmetic per-waypoint label bug. The label bug (if present here
# too) is a separate WebATM frontend issue, not something to compensate for in this file.
#
# WAYPOINT FIX (VAG628): removed the old "008" fix (21.220848,105.807978) -- after VAG628007
# (21.221523,105.805618, kept as-is per real trajectory), the route now goes straight to the
# on-centerline point 21.2200,105.8110, then turns right into what was already the next point
# (21.220291,105.809758). Net effect: one point fewer between 007 and the turn.
#
# KNOWN ISSUE (not fixed, reverted): BlueSky auto-deletes any aircraft the instant it reaches the LAST
# waypoint of its LNAV route (bluesky/traffic/autopilot.py ~line 168-175, unconditional -- ignores any
# later DEL time in this file). Both arrivals here disappear right after reaching their gate rather
# than at their scripted DEL time. Tried fixing this on the VVDN scenario (see that file's header for
# the full story) with a dummy extra waypoint + "AT <lastwp> DO LNAV OFF" -- confirmed via live
# telemetry that it does not reliably stop the aircraft and can even cause a runaway negative altitude.
# Reverted as not worth the added risk for what's a cosmetic timing issue -- each aircraft still
# correctly reaches and briefly sits at its gate before disappearing, just earlier than the scripted DEL.
#
# ---- HVN7560 arrival milestones (real trace, RWY11L, verified stop ~77m from real Gate 24) ----
#  10:55:14  TOUCHDOWN     21.222420,105.802561  0ft   124kt  hdg107
#  10:55:49  1st turn      21.220001,105.810063         9.5kt hdg149
#  10:58:26  long straight 21.217090,105.803668        18kt  hdg287
#  10:59:25  2nd turn zone 21.216834,105.800845         9.5kt hdg166
#  11:00:40  STOP (Gate24) 21.216089,105.801112         0kt
#
# ---- VAG628 arrival milestones (real trace, RWY11L, verified stop ~87m from real Gate 24) ----
#  03:17:09  TOUCHDOWN     21.222839,105.801137  0ft  124kt  hdg108
#  03:17:50  1st turn      21.220291,105.809758        13.5kt hdg113
#  03:20:40  long straight 21.216545,105.805406        15kt  hdg287
#  03:22:02  2nd turn zone 21.216808,105.802247         5.5kt hdg194
#  03:28:59  STOP (Gate24) 21.216648,105.802193         0kt

00:00:00.00>TRAILS ON
00:00:00.00>ASAS ON

